ant status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>TOKORO, MASAHARU</name></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>TSUNOGAE, YASUO</name></addressbook></applicant></applicants><inventors><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>SAKAMOTO MASATO</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>TAGUCHI KAZUNORI</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>TOKORO MASAHARU</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>TSUNOGAE YASUO</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>SAKAMOTO, MASATO</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>TAGUCHI, KAZUNORI</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>TOKORO, MASAHARU</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>TSUNOGAE, YASUO</name></addressbook></inventor></inventors></parties></bibliographic-data><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="EN"><p>A process for producing a hydrogenated ring-opening polymerization polymer which comprises the step of polymerizing a cycloolefin through ring-opening polymerization in the presence of a polymerization catalyst comprising an organoruthenium compound or an organoosmium compound and the step of hydrogenating the carbon-carbon double bonds of the ring-opening polymerization polymer by adding a hydrogenation catalyst and hydrogen to the reaction system resulting from the polymerization step. When the polymerization catalyst comprising an organoruthenium compound or an organoosmium compound further contains a heteroatom-containing carbene compound, it shows higher activity in the ring-opening polymerization.</p></abstract><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="FR"><p>La présente invention concerne un procédé de production d'un polymère de polymérisation hydrogéné à chaîne ouverte, consistant à polymériser une cyclo-oléfine par polymérisation à chaîne ouverte en présence d'un catalyseur de polymérisation contenant un composé d'organoruthénium ou un composé d'organo-osmium, et à hydrogéner les liaisons doubles carbone-carbone du polymère de polymérisation à chaîne ouverte en ajoutant un catalyseur d'hydrogénation et un hydrogène au système réactif obtenu de l'opération de polymérisation. Lorsque le catalyseur de polymérisation comprenant un composé d'organoruthénium ou un composé d'organo-osmium contient également un composé de carbène, il connaît alors une activité plus élevée au cours de la polymérisation à chaîne ouverte.</p></abstract><copyright>User acknowledges that the Information Retrieval Facility (IRF) and its third party providers retain all right, title and interest in and to this xml under applicable copyright laws. User acquires no ownership rights to this xml including but not limited to its format. User hereby accepts the terms and conditions of the Licence Agreement set forth at http://www.ir-facility.org/legal/marec/data_licence</copyright></patent-document>